        "body": "<p>Kelly McColgan has 25 years of hairdressing experience and is qualified in trichology, the science of hair and scalp health.</p><p>She started at twelve years old in Ireland, sweeping floors in a salon because she wanted to be in one. She trained in Belfast, then cut her way around the world before landing on the Gold Coast.</p><p>Somewhere in those 25 years she got tired of a particular conversation. A woman would sit down, worried about her hair, and be sold something longer, fuller and faker. Nobody would tell her why it was happening. Kelly went and studied the science so she could answer the question instead of decorating it.</p><p>That is why Silk is both things at once. It is a clinic, with a microscope and real answers about what your hair is doing. It is also a Friday morning with rollers in and an iced coffee in your hand.</p><p>Both are the same thing, really. Because when your hair feels right, it helps you feel right.</p>",
